From: Duy Truong <duytruong@google.com>
Date: Thu, 21 May 2026 11:31:47 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Fix heap underflow write in ft_smooth_raster_lcd

This patch fixes a vulnerability in FreeType's LCD rasterizer where a
short truncation when computing spans' x-coordinate leads to a heap
underflow write. We add bounds checks in ft_smooth_raster_lcd and
ft_smooth_raster_lcdv to reject outlines that are too wide or too
high, similar to the existing guard in ft_smooth_raster_overlap.

This was autogenerated by MendIt (go/androidmendit)

Bug: 506109174
Test: m libft2
Flag: EXEMPT BUGFIX
Change-Id: If87af623a07ed59d30e31097c5507834500c47d0
---
 src/smooth/ftsmooth.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/smooth/ftsmooth.c b/src/smooth/ftsmooth.c
index f0acc1ea4..06a1e1c6f 100644
--- a/src/smooth/ftsmooth.c
+++ b/src/smooth/ftsmooth.c
@@ -141,6 +141,10 @@
     TOrigin            target;
 
 
+    /* Reject outlines too wide for 16-bit FT_Span.x — see ft_smooth_raster_overlap. */
+    if ( bitmap->width / 3 > 0x7FFF )
+      return FT_THROW( Raster_Overflow );
+
     /* Render 3 separate coverage bitmaps, shifting the outline.  */
     /* Set up direct rendering to record them on each third byte. */
     params.source     = outline;
@@ -208,6 +212,10 @@
     FT_Raster_Params  params;
 
 
+    /* Reject outlines too high — see ft_smooth_raster_overlap. */
+    if ( bitmap->rows / 3 > 0x7FFF )
+      return FT_THROW( Raster_Overflow );
+
     params.target = bitmap;
     params.source = outline;
     params.flags  = FT_RASTER_FLAG_AA;
